SUMMARY:Celebrate Abilities Free Concert
DESCRIPTION:Join St. James Episcopal Church for the inaugural performance of the ‘Celebrate Abilities’ Concert Series\, in honor of Disability Pride Month. \nThis all-ages\, inclusive musical performance will feature award-winning singer-songwriter Halley Elwell and The Unsinkables\, Schreiber’s modern band and beautiful artwork from the artists of ASPIE. \nHalley Elwell is a singer-songwriter whose evocative music blends elements of jazz\, folk\, pop\, and rock. Known for her rich voice and insightful lyrics\, Elwell’s music has been featured on radio and television and in apps and has been recognized by ASCAP and the John Lennon Songwriting Contest. In 2025\, she undertook her biggest project yet\, a memoir-style concept album and podcast called Spontaneous Mutation. \nBased on her experiences living with neurofibromatosis\, the project explores chronic illness\, the facial difference movement\, disability\, and the importance of telling new stories about all of them. Elwell is a member of Recording Artists and Music Professionals with Disabilities (RAMPD). Click here to learn more about the concert series.
URL:https://apostlesucc.org/event/celebrate-abilities-free-concert/
LOCATION:Saint James Episcopal Church\, 119 N. Duke St\, Lancaster\, PA\, 17602\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://apostlesucc.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Celebrate-Abilities-Concert-Flyer_July-19-26-1-scaled.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Figlancaster": "https://figlancaster.com/event/celebrate-abilities-concert-series/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:figlancaster
X-SOURCE:Fig Lancaster
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260719T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260719T163000
DTSTAMP:20260601T133754Z
CREATED:20260601T132627Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260601T133754Z
UID:10014718-1784473200-1784478600@figlancaster.com
SUMMARY:Celebrate Abilities Concert Series
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the inaugural performance of the ‘Celebrate Abilities’ Concert Series\, in honor of Disability Pride Month. This all ages\, inclusive musical performance will feature award-winning singer-songwriter Halley Elwell and The Unsinkables\, Schreiber’s modern band.\n\nAbout Halley Elwell\n\nHalley Elwellis an award-winning singer-songwriter whose evocative music blends elements of jazz\, folk\, pop\, and rock. Known for her rich voice and insightful lyrics\, Elwell’s music has been featured on radio and television and in apps and has been recognized by ASCAP and the John Lennon Songwriting Contest. In 2025\, she undertook her biggest project yet\, a memoir-style concept album and podcast called Spontaneous Mutation. Based on her experiences living with neurofibromatosis\, the project explores chronic illness\, the facial difference movement\, disability\, and the importance of telling new stories about all of them. Elwell is a member of RAMPD (Recording Artists and Music Professionals with Disabilities).\n\nAbout the Location\n\nSaint James Episcopal Church offers accessible entrances for individuals of all abilities. There will be an accessible drop-off zone in front of Saint James and accessible parking nearby in the Duke and Christian Street garages. A live broadcast and sensory spaces will be available during the performance. \n\nAbout the Sponsors\n\nThe Celebrate Abilities Concert Series is presented by Saint James Episcopal Church\, The Urban Well and Schreiber Center for Pediatric Development with funding from Lancaster MusicFest. \n            \n        \n                \n                \n    Learn More
URL:https://figlancaster.com/event/celebrate-abilities-concert-series/
LOCATION:Saint James Episcopal Church\, 119 North Duke Street\, Lancaster\, PA\, 17602\, United States
CATEGORIES:Arts & Entertainment
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://fig.guide/content/uploads/sites/3/2026/06/Celebrate-Abilities-FB-Post.avif
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Figlancaster": "https://figlancaster.com/event/w-miller-barbour-a-lancaster-county-leader-for-human-rights/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:figlancaster
X-SOURCE:Fig Lancaster
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260719T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260719T163000
DTSTAMP:20260626T124534Z
CREATED:20260625T222044Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260626T124534Z
UID:10014761-1784473200-1784478600@figlancaster.com
SUMMARY:W. Miller Barbour: A Lancaster County Leader For Human Rights
DESCRIPTION:Join historian Eric Schubert for a fascinating presentation on W. Miller Barbour (1908–1957)\, a Lancaster County leader whose work in social work\, civil rights\, and community activism helped lay the groundwork for the Civil Rights Movement. \n\n\n\n A graduate of Elizabethtown College and one of the first African American college football players in Lancaster County\, Barbour went on to earn an advanced degree in social work and became a leader in efforts to combat gang violence and promote racial and economic justice through his work with the National Urban League in Denver and Los Angeles. Although Barbour died in 1957 before the passage of major civil rights legislation\, his work anticipated many of the reforms and social changes that would define the movement in the decades that followed. This program sheds light on the life of a remarkable but often overlooked local leader whose impact reached far beyond Lancaster County. \n\n\n\n\n    Learn More
URL:https://figlancaster.com/event/w-miller-barbour-a-lancaster-county-leader-for-human-rights/
LOCATION:Thaddeus Stevens College of Technology\, 750 E. King St.\, Lancaster\, 17603
CATEGORIES:Community
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://fig.guide/content/uploads/sites/3/2026/06/Screenshot-2026-06-25-174238.avif
ORGANIZER;CN="African American Historical Society of South Central Pennsylvania":MAILTO:information@aahsscpa.org
END:VEVENT
