BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lancaster Libraries": "https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/lego-block-party-172197"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lancaster_libraries
SUMMARY:Lego Block Party!
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260727T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260727T190000
UID:54b55a8e8976746d4f63596fddc5e591@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:STEM\, Summer Reading\, Children\, Tweens\n\nThe LEGO Block Pa
 rty at the library is a fun and creative program where children ages 8-12 
 come together to build various creations using LEGO bricks. Participants o
 ften have the opportunity to work individually or in teams to design and c
 onstruct imaginative structures\, vehicles\, and scenes based on a theme o
 r their own imagination. The club typically fosters collaboration\, proble
 m-solving\, and fine motor skills while encouraging a love for building an
 d creativity. It's a great way for community members to socialize\, learn\
 , and have fun in a supportive environment.Registration for Lego Block Par
 ty will open at 9:00AM on Wednesday\, July 15th for Manheim Township and E
 ast Lampeter residents and on Wednesday\, July 22nd for residents of other
  municipalities.For youth ages 8-12 years of age only.Designated Ages –
  Please adhere to the age restrictions designated on your registration. 
 Only children in that age range will be admitted.   Cancellations- Ple
 ase check your email prior to departing to verify that the program has not
  been cancelled. Library Program PoliciesNo Show – Patrons failing to ca
 ncel their registration for more than 2 library programs in a month will b
 e restricted from registering for future programs for a period of one mont
 h’s time. Please cancel your registrations at least 2 hours prior to the
  start of the program to allow for those on the waiting list to be notifie
 d of their change in registration status.Late Arrivals – Please arrive 1
 0 minutes prior to the start of the program to allow for parking and other
  circumstances. The program will begin promptly at the designated time. At
  this time\, your spot will be forfeited to those on the wait list who wil
 l be granted entry. If spots remain\, registrants may be allowed into the 
 program. However\, registrants will not be permitted to enter the program 
 5 minutes past the start time.Check In - All participants must provide an 
 emergency contact number upon registration or at the start of the program.
LOCATION:Manheim Township\, MTP Morgan Center C
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/lego-block-party-172197
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lancaster Libraries": "https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/oh-captain-my-captain-tweens-165976"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lancaster_libraries
SUMMARY:Oh Captain My Captain! For Tweens
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260727T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260727T190000
UID:41be1db81d7ecf7ebcb7ef3db640c613@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Gaming\, Tweens\n\nOh Captain\, My Captain! is a short form wo
 rld-building role-playing game (RPG) that explores heroism and the complic
 ated relationships we have with people we admire. The game revolves around
  players drawing from a deck of cards with open-ended questions. Each ques
 tion players answer helps them learn about their character\, their world\,
  their captain and the complicated relationship they have with a living le
 gend. Players use these answers to make connections between their stories 
 leading up one of three final questions that end the game. No experience o
 r prep needed! Ages 10-12.
LOCATION:Ephrata\, EPH 1/2 Multipurpose Room Kitchen Side
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/oh-captain-my-captain-tw
 eens-165976
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lancaster Libraries": "https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/succulents-166600"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lancaster_libraries
SUMMARY:Succulents
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260727T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260727T190000
UID:163e996da27988f760db970d9e705105@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Community\, Summer Reading\, Adults\n\nSusan Hotham from the P
 enn State Extension Master Gardeners will present a program about succulen
 ts. She’ll describe the main families of succulents\, including Cactacea
 e\, as well as favorites including those that may be planted outdoors in P
 ennsylvania. Directions on how to grow and propagate succulents is include
 d\, as well as growing from seeds. We’ll also have a hands-on take-home 
 activity. Ages 16+.
LOCATION:Ephrata\, EPH 1/2 Multipurpose Room Projector Side
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/succulents-166600
