SUMMARY:Vertebrates & Invertebrates with Lancaster County Parks Naturalist
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260806T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260806T153000
UID:e6630b5198e559a9763e7ce0d042fdd9@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Community\, Discussion\, Presentation\, Storytime\, Summer Rea
 ding\, Toddlers\, Children\, Tweens\n\nRescheduled Program Alert!Our Verte
 brates and Invertebrates program\, originally scheduled for June 15th\, ha
 s been rescheduled for Thursday\, August 6th at 2:30 PM.We invite you to j
 oin us for this rescheduled presentation!Discover the amazing world of ani
 mals by looking at what’s inside! Animals with a sturdy backbone and a s
 keleton are called vertebrates\, like leaping frogs\, soaring birds\, and 
 even you.On the flip side\, invertebrates are the "spineless" superstars o
 f nature—like wiggly worms and crunchy beetles—who make up almost all 
 the animals on Earth! Whether they have a hard outer shell for protection 
 or a flexible body for squishing into tiny spaces\, every animal has a spe
 cial shape that helps it survive and thrive in the wild.
LOCATION:Manheim Community\, MAN Kreider Cultural Center
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/vertebrates-invertebrate
 s-lancaster-county-parks-naturalist-172145
