 shine - if it's raining\, we'll be meeting indoors and limit our outside t
 ime.)  We'll get our hands dirty in the planters\, do some crafts\, and ma
 ybe even read a story!  We'll supply\, the tools\, gloves\, and the plante
 rs.  Plan on getting a little dirty.  This program is designed for childre
 n ages 6 - 9 years old.  Designated Ages – Please adhere to the age re
 strictions designated on your registration. Only children in that age rang
 e will be admitted.   Registration will open at 9:00AM on Wednesday\, 
 June 10th for Manheim Township and East Lampeter residents and on Wednesda
 y\, June 17th for residents of other municipalities.Drop Off Program –
  This program is intended for children over the age of 6 years who can p
 articipate independently. Adult(s) must be present to check in child with 
 youth services staff prior to program. Adults will not be allowed in the e
 vent space.  *For children ages 6–7\, this is a drop-off program\; h
 owever\, a parent or caregiver must remain in the library for the durati
 on of the program. Library Program Policies No Show – Patrons failing 
 to cancel their registration for more than 2 library programs in a month w
 ill be restricted from registering for future programs for a period of one
  month’s time. Please cancel your registrations at least 2 hours prior t
 o the start of the program to allow those on the waiting list to be notifi
 ed of their change in registration status. Late Arrivals – Please arri
 ve 10 minutes prior to the start of the program to allow for parking a
 nd other circumstances. The program will begin promptly at the designated 
 time. At this time\, your spot will be forfeited to those on the wait list
  who will be granted entry. If spots remain\, registrants may be allowed i
 nto the program. However\, registrants will not be permitted to enter 
 the program 5 minutes past the start time. Photography - The Manheim Towns
 hip Public Library Code of Conduct Policy prohibits photographing or video
  recording individuals (including children) without their consent (or in t
 he case of a child\, the consent of a parent or guardian).
